    <sectiondef kind="user-defined">
      <header>Debug message configuration.</header>
      <description><para>Controls the amount of information printed to the Serial Monitor for each module and globally. If the debug level is 0, all debug macros are defined as empty. The compiler will optimize and remove them from the final code, saving memory.</para>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>0 = No debugging. Saves memory and makes the program faster.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>1 = Errors (ERROR): Shows only critical messages.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>2 = Warnings (WARN): Shows errors and important warnings.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>3 = Information (INFO): Shows general program flow (recommended for normal debugging).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>4 = Verbose (VERBOSE): Shows very detailed information, such as sensor readings every 5s. </para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
</description>
